      "id": "I_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABDaW6dw",
      "title": "Security Analysis: 11 potential vulnerabilities detected in superchain-ops",
      "author": "0xRAMlabs",
      "number": 1431,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "body": "Hi 👋\n\nWe are **[0xRAM Labs](https://0xram.com)**, a Web3 security research firm. Our automated security scanner analyzed the smart contracts in this repository and identified **11 potential vulnerabilities**.\n\n### 🔍 Summary of Findings\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Total Issues | 11 |\n| Highest Severity | High |\n| Top Finding | Denial of Service (DoS) via unbounded array loop |\n\n### 🚨 Most Critical Finding\n\n**Denial of Service (DoS) via unbounded array loop** (`High`)\n> Line 206 contains a `for` loop that appears to iterate over the length of a dynamic array. If the array grows too large, the gas cost to execute the loop will exceed the block gas limit, causing the function to become permanently unusable.\n\nThis is just a preview — the full analysis covers all 11 findings with detailed remediation guidance.\n\n### 📊 Full Security Report\n\nWe've generated a detailed, interactive security report for your review:\n\n👉 **[View Full Report](https://0xram.com/report/report-4r9xsj04r)**\n\n### 🛡️ How We Can Help\n\nIf you'd like a comprehensive manual audit by our senior security researchers, we'd be happy to discuss:\n\n- **[Book a Free Consultation](https://0xram.com/contact)**\n- **Email**: [audit@0xram.com](mailto:audit@0xram.com)\n\n---\n*This analysis was performed by 0xRAM Labs' automated security scanner. For questions or to opt out of future scans, please contact us at audit@0xram.com.*\n",
